n Mysore Lancer Lines in 1955, and 2026 is its 72nd year. Claims to have introduced the theme-puja concept to Bengaluru in 2014; runs 'Muktangan' for emerging artists. Ladies Club premises, Jayamahal Extension, next to Jayamahal Park, Bengaluru 560046 North Bangalore Cultural Samithi (NBCS) / Bangalore Kali Bari 1978 The third-oldest Puja in the city, after Ulsoor (1950) and Jayamahal (1955). One of very few Bengali bodies in Bengaluru with a permanent Kali temple rather than only an annual pandal. Deccan Herald (25 Sept 2025) reported its 48th Durga Puja at Nagavara, which matches a 1978 founding. The temple is at Nandini Layout and the Puja is held at Nagavara. Kali Bari temple at Nandini Layout, Bengaluru 560096; 2025 Durga Puja pandal at Nagavara Socio Cultural Association, Indiranagar (SCA) Conflicting, c. 1967 (its own 2025 '58 years' claim) or c. 1970 (Citykemp 2015, '45 years old') Indiranagar's long-running Puja, started by Bengali residents of Indiranagar, Domlur and Ulsoor on the initiative of the late Dilu Sen, then a manager at Tata Steel. Also runs Lakshmi, Kali and Saraswati Puja and Poila Boishakh. Still active. The founding year is not recorded anywhere we could reach. Sishu Griha and Poorna Prajna School Grounds, HAL III Stage / New Thippasandra, Indiranagar Sarathi Socio-Cultural Trust, Koramangala First Puja 2003; formally registered 2006 The city's largest-footfall Puja, claiming 1.5-2 lakh visitors; its five-day cultural festival is branded 'Sammad'. Won the Senco Sharod Samman 2018 for ambience and crowd management. Caution, a separate 'Sarathi Cultural Association' with a different Koramangala venue also exists - do not merge the two. Mangala Kalyana Mantapa, 80 ft Road near Forum Mall, KHB 7th Block, Koramangala Kolaj Socio-Cultural Trust, Koramangala 2010 Deliberately 'ghoroa' - homely and intimate rather than mega-scale. Strongly concept-driven idols, e.g. Durga as ascetic Brahmacharini rather than warrior. Free entry, no parking. No standalone website. Sri Krishna Temple, near Jyothi Nivas College, Koramangala, Bengaluru 560034 Whitefield Cultural Association (WCA) 2003 Runs the trademarked 'Whitefield Durga Puja'. Registered under the Government of Karnataka, with an explicit CSR arm in education, healthcare and environment. The family-oriented East Bengaluru Puja. Whitefield; 2025 venue Palm Meadows, near Mahaveer Tranquil SORRBA - Sarjapur Outer Ring Road Bengali Association 2008 (news-sourced, not primary) Formed by Bengali families living around the junction of Sarjapur Road and the Outer Ring Road. Heavy on Bengali theatre productions and Kolkata street-food stalls alongside the Puja. The 2008 date is from a 2015 Citykemp feature; SORRBA's own site does not state a year. Sarjapur Road; 2025 venue Samskruti Pavilion Convention Centre, Sulikunte BARSHA - Bengali Association for HSR and Sarjapur, Bangalore December 2014 Its own about page says 'We started our journey in December, 2014', corroborated by Karnataka society registration number JNR-S344-2014-15. Aggregators variously claim 2016 and 2019 - both appear wrong. Grew from 20 to 125 members; runs Rabindra-Nazrul Jayanti at The HSR Club; CSR work with Samarthanam Trust. BARSHA Durga Puja Ground, opposite TCIS School, HSR Extension / Haralur, off Sarjapur Road ECCA - Electronic City Cultural Association 2012 The IT-corridor Puja, run largely by tech-professional volunteers; a registered charitable organisation formed in 2012, with its first Sarvajanin Durgotsav the same year. Large award haul. No official website - a page at sumandeyashi.github.io is a personal build, not ECCA's site. White Feather Convention Centre, near NICE Toll Gate, Electronic City Sanskritik Bengali Association Bangalore c. 2013-2014 (approximate; site says 'Celebrating 11 Glorious Years' but gives no year) This is the real organisation behind what people call 'Sanskriti Bangalore' - no body of that exact name exists. A non-profit trust started by South Bangalore families; won Sharod Samman Best Theme Puja 2018 and Best Venue Branding 2018. Founding year approximate. Elite Banquet Hall, Puttenahalli Road, JP Nagar Phase 6, Bengaluru 560078 Anandadhara Bangalore Conflicting, founded 2011 (Citykemp 2015) or registered 2012 (other sources) Explicitly themed around rural Bengal rather than urban spectacle. Founded around 2011 and registered the following year, by the accounts available. JP Nagar, South Bengaluru R T Nagar Bengali Socio Cultural Trust (R T Nagar Sarbajanin Durga Puja Samiti) 2006 The Palace Grounds Puja. One of the few that runs Jagadhatri Puja as well as Saraswati, Durga, Kali and Lakshmi. Blood-donation camps, hosts around 50 NGO children, wheelchair access for seniors, and its own mobile app. 'R T Nagar Bengali Association' and the Samiti are the same body, not two organisations. Puja at Palace Grounds, Gate 9 (Princess Green), Bellary Road; registered at No. 17, 10th Cross, Manorayanapalya, Sultanpalya Main Road, R T Nagar PO, Bengaluru 560032 Oikotan Hebbal Cultural Society 2013 Runs all four Pujas - Durga, Kali, Lakshmi and Saraswati. Repeat winner of best-theme awards; named by Deccan Herald among 2025's notable pandals. The domain oikotan.in only redirects to Facebook, so the Facebook page is the real address. Hebbal, North Bengaluru Kaggadasapura Bengali Association (KBA) 15 August 2007 Claims 6,500+ members. Its Puja is branded 'Sharad Utsav'. Notable for us because its catchment, C V Raman Nagar, is named after the same physicist who founded RRI and directed IISc. V K Sports Convention Hall, Malleshpalya; serves Kaggadasapura and C V Raman Nagar Bengali in Bangalore (BinB) 2004 Started as an online Bengali community and is unusually broad, BinB Sports (badminton, table tennis, a football league, gully cricket), BinB JobMart, and Kannada Rajyotsava alongside the Bengali calendar. Deccan Herald covered its 15th Durgotsav, honouring Tagore. The 2004 date is on its membership page, not its homepage. Durgotsav at Chandrodaya Convention Centre, Dairy Circle; registered office at WorkFlo, Ranka Junction, Dooravani Nagar, Bengaluru 560016 Jagriti Bongiyo Cultural Association (JBCA) 2014 Formed by Bengali families around RM Nagar and TC Palya; society registration DRO/SJN/SOR/119/14-15. Social and environmental themes. The spelling varies across its own channels - Bangiya, Bangiyo, Bongiyo. ITI Hockey Ground, beside K R Puram Hanging Bridge Begur Bengali Socio-Cultural Trust (BBSCT) 2023 One of the newest, and unusually transparent about its legal status - Trust Registration BGR-4-00003-2023-2, Darpan KA/2023/0346089, 12AA and 80G effective FY 2023-24, so donations are tax-exempt. Pairs the Puja with education, healthcare and environment work. Begur, South-East Bengaluru Vivekananda Cultural Association (VCA), Yelahanka Founded April 2002 by a 42-member team; registered 2004 The Yelahanka-area Bengali association, running a year-round Bengali festival calendar for the New Town diaspora. Both years come from the indexed text of its own site, corroborated by a 2013 Bengaluru Puja blog. Yelahanka New Town, Bengaluru SmaranniK (Bengali theatre group) 2012 The only Bengali theatre group regularly performing at Ranga Shankara, and it runs its own annual SmaranniK Theatre Festival. Director Sayandeb Bhattacharya; has travelled to 15 festivals. The strongest candidate if the Puja wants a Bengali stage production. Performs at Ranga Shankara, JP Nagar If your association or Puja belongs on this list and is not here, tell a convenor and it goes up. We only list organisations whose details we could actually verify. No prior experience needed across any role Just your love for Durga Puja, and that familiar ache of missing home, are more than enough. People who had never tied a bamboo joint have built the pandal. People who could not read Bengali have served bhog to four hundred people in an hour. কোনো পূর্ব অভিজ্ঞতার দরকার নেই। শুধু পুজোর প্রতি ভালোবাসা আর সেই চেনা বুকের টান, “এই সময়ে বাড়িতে থাকলে ভালো হতো”, সেটুকুই যথেষ্ট। Volunteer form Join the WhatsApp group Talk to a convenor Tathagata Ghosh General Secretary +91 7890825610 Devraj Karmakar Convenor +91 7384859512 Sirshendu Pathak Convenor +91 7001453229</data>
</node>
<node id="team:68c16c941c3f">
  <data key="d0">VolunteerTeam</data>
  <data key="d14">Logistics</data>
  <data key="d15">লজিস্টিকস</data>
  <data key="d9">যোগদান Join us A Puja was never one person's work পুজো হয় সবার মিলিত প্রার্থনায় Eight teams, and not one of them asks for experience. What is actually required is time in October and the willingness to be told what to do by someone two years junior to you. Fill the volunteer form 🎨 কন্টেন্ট ও ডিজাইন Content &amp; Design Turn creativity into devotion. Social posts, banners, storytelling, visual design, the Puja gets its face from your hands. সৃজনশীলতাকে পুজোর রূপ দাও। সোশাল মিডিয়া পোস্ট থেকে ব্যানার, গল্প বলা থেকে ভিজ্যুয়াল ডিজাইন, তোমার হাতের ছোঁয়ায় পুজো পাক তার পরিচয়। 💼 স্পনসরশিপ Sponsorship Be the bridge between the celebration and the world around it. Connect, communicate, and help build the resources that bring Durgotsab to life. পুজোর আয়োজনকে সম্ভব করে তোলার পেছনে থাকে অনেক মানুষের সংযোগ। সেই সেতু হয়ে ওঠো তুমি। 🌸 সাজসজ্জা Decoration Sharad has its own language, marigolds, earthen lamps, the golden haze of autumn. No experience needed, only willing hands. শরতের নিজের একটা ভাষা আছে, গাঁদা ফুলের মালা, মাটির প্রদীপ, সোনালি আলোর ছায়া। সেই ভাষায় সাজাও আমাদের মণ্ডপ। 🪔 পুজোর আয়োজন Puja Arrangements The sacred heart of it all. Flowers, incense, dhuno, mantra, the conch, from Bodhon to Bisarjan. This is not work, it is worship. এটি সবচেয়ে পবিত্র ভূমিকা, ফুল, ধূপ, ধুনো, মন্ত্র, শঙ্খধ্বনি, বোধন থেকে বিসর্জন। এটি শুধু কাজ নয়, এটি আরাধনা। 💰 ফান্ডরেইজিং Fundraising Desks outside the mess counters three weeks before the Puja. Chat with peers, spread the festive mood, mobilise the campus. পুজোর ঠিক তিন সপ্তাহ আগে মেসে বসে শিক্ষার্থীদের সাথে গল্পে-আড্ডায় অনুদান সংগ্রহের দায়িত্ব। 📦 লজিস্টিকস Logistics Pandal build, sound, lighting, procurement, venue execution, the backbone that keeps five days of festivity running. মণ্ডপ তৈরি, সাউন্ড, লাইটিং থেকে শুরু করে পুজোর যাবতীয় সরঞ্জামের পরিচালনা, পেছনের সারির মাস্টারমাইন্ড। 📖 স্মারকপত্র ও ম্যাগাজিন Magazine, Probash Capture the magic in words, art and nostalgia. Curate, edit and lay out our annual souvenir so campus memories outlive us. লেখা, ছবি ও স্মৃতির কোলাজে আমাদের পুজোর নিজস্ব ম্যাগাজিন সাজিয়ে তোলার কাজ। 🥣 ভোগ ও প্রসাদ বিতরণ Bhog &amp; Prasad Serve Ma's khichuri bhog and prasad with affection. Be the hospitality of the festival; nobody leaves without a blessing. মায়ের মহাপ্রসাদ ও খিচুড়ি ভোগ ভক্তি আর ভালোবাসায় সবার মাঝে বিতরণ করার পবিত্র দায়িত্ব। নিমন্ত্রণ The invitation The gate is open, and we mean it সবার জন্য খোলা A Puja that only its own campus attends is a private party with incense. These are the neighbours we would like in the queue for bhog, the research institutions around us, and the Bengali organisations who have been keeping this city's Pujo going far longer than we have. Research institutions nearby NCBS 1991 National Centre for Biological Sciences, Tata Institute of Fundamental Research A campus where people chase fruit flies down corridors to find out how memory works, map the monsoon's effect on frog song, and keep a natural-history archive of India - biology at every scale from a single molecule to a whole ecosystem. GKVK Campus, Bellary Road, Bengaluru 560065 JNCASR 1989 Jawaharlal Nehru Centre for Advanced Scientific Research A small, deliberately un-departmental institute where a chemist, a geneticist and a fluid dynamicist share a corridor - set up in Nehru's birth-centenary year and built around the idea that the interesting science happens where the subjects collide. Jakkur, Bengaluru 560064 - about 11 km from the IISc campus ICTS-TIFR 2007 International Centre for Theoretical Sciences, Tata Institute of Fundamental Research A hillside campus built for the specific purpose of putting string theorists, climate modellers, mathematicians and cell biologists in the same building for a month at a time, and seeing what comes out. Survey No. 151, Shivakote, Hesaraghatta Hobli, Bengaluru 560089 RRI 1948 Raman Research Institute The institute a Nobel laureate built for himself because he refused to stop working - today it points radio telescopes at the early universe, watches liquid crystals misbehave, and still keeps Raman's own collection of gemstones and iridescent beetles. C. V. Raman Avenue, Sadashivanagar, Bengaluru 560080 IIA 1971 Indian Institute of Astrophysics India's oldest scientific institution by descent - a lineage running from a colonial Madras observatory of 1786 to a telescope at 4,500 m in Ladakh that astronomers in Koramangala operate over the internet. II Block, Koramangala, Bengaluru 560034 TIFR-CAM 2007 TIFR Centre for Applicable Mathematics A small, intense mathematics centre for the kind of equations that describe real things - fluids, waves, control systems, the shape of an optimal solution. P.B. No. 6503, Sharada Nagar, Chikkabommasandra, Yelahanka, Bengaluru 560065 BLiSC Bangalore Life Science Cluster Four institutes sharing one fence, one set of microscopes and one canteen, fundamental biology, stem-cell medicine, a start-up incubator and a genetics-for-society institute, all on the same north-Bengaluru field. GKVK Campus, Bellary Road, Bengaluru 560065 - the NCBS site inStem 2009 Institute for Stem Cell Science and Regenerative Medicine An institute trying to persuade cells to rebuild what disease took away - heart, nerve, skin - and to grow human disease in a dish so it can be argued with. GKVK Campus, Bellary Road, Bengaluru 560065 C-CAMP 2009 Centre for Cellular and Molecular Platforms The place where a life-science idea goes to become a company - shared million-rupee instruments, and one of India's busiest biotech incubators. GKVK Campus, Bellary Road, Bengaluru 560065 TIGS 2017 Tata Institute for Genetics and Society Genetics pointed squarely at Indian problems - malaria-carrying mosquitoes, rare inherited disease, and crops that have to survive an Indian summer. NCBS/inStem campus, GKVK, Bellary Road, Bengaluru 560065 URSC 1972 U R Rao Satellite Centre, ISRO The building where India's satellites are actually screwed together - more than a hundred of them so far, for communications, navigation, weather, Earth observation and trips to the Moon and Mars. Old Airport Road, Vimanapura Post, Bengaluru 560017 CSIR-NAL 1959 CSIR-National Aerospace Laboratories India's only civilian aerospace laboratory - home of the Saras and Hansa aircraft, and of wind tunnels big enough to walk into, where everything from a fighter's wing to a bridge deck gets put in front of a very large fan. HAL Airport Road, Kodihalli, Bengaluru 560017; second campus at Belur IIIT-B 1998 International Institute of Information Technology Bangalore A graduate school planted deliberately in the middle of Electronic City, close enough to the software industry that the faculty and the customers share a traffic jam. 26/C, Electronics City Phase 1, Hosur Road, Bengaluru 560100 ISI Bangalore 1978 Indian Statistical Institute, Bangalore Centre Thirty acres of eucalyptus on the Mysore Road where pure mathematicians and statisticians work on everything from operator algebras to how India counts itself. 8th Mile, Mysore Road, RVCE Post, Bengaluru 560059 Bengali Bengaluru The Bengalee Association held this city's first Sarbojanin Durga Puja in 1950. Our Puja is three years old. We are the youngest people in this room and we know it. The Bengalee Association, Bangalore Puja from 1950; association registered 16 September 1959 The city's oldest Bengali association, and the one that matters most to us, its first Sarbojanin Durga Puja in 1950 was, in its own words, 'held under the initiatives and tutelage of a few Professors of the Indian Institute of Science, Bangalore'. One of the very few with a permanent cultural centre rather than an annual pandal - land allotted April 1977, building inaugurated 4 April 1980. The Puja dates from 1950 and the association was registered in 1959. Tagore Cultural Centre, 1/A Assaye Road, Sivanchetti Gardens, Ulsoor, Bengaluru 560042 Jayamahal Cultural Association (JCA) 1955 The city's second-oldest Puja - the first was held in a vacant building in Mysore Lancer Lines in 1955, and 2026 is its 72nd year. Claims to have introduced the theme-puja concept to Bengaluru in 2014; runs 'Muktangan' for emerging artists. Ladies Club premises, Jayamahal Extension, next to Jayamahal Park, Bengaluru 560046 North Bangalore Cultural Samithi (NBCS) / Bangalore Kali Bari 1978 The third-oldest Puja in the city, after Ulsoor (1950) and Jayamahal (1955). One of very few Bengali bodies in Bengaluru with a permanent Kali temple rather than only an annual pandal. Deccan Herald (25 Sept 2025) reported its 48th Durga Puja at Nagavara, which matches a 1978 founding. The temple is at Nandini Layout and the Puja is held at Nagavara. Kali Bari temple at Nandini Layout, Bengaluru 560096; 2025 Durga Puja pandal at Nagavara Socio Cultural Association, Indiranagar (SCA) Conflicting, c. 1967 (its own 2025 '58 years' claim) or c. 1970 (Citykemp 2015, '45 years old') Indiranagar's long-running Puja, started by Bengali residents of Indiranagar, Domlur and Ulsoor on the initiative of the late Dilu Sen, then a manager at Tata Steel. Also runs Lakshmi, Kali and Saraswati Puja and Poila Boishakh. Still active. The founding year is not recorded anywhere we could reach. Sishu Griha and Poorna Prajna School Grounds, HAL III Stage / New Thippasandra, Indiranagar Sarathi Socio-Cultural Trust, Koramangala First Puja 2003; formally registered 2006 The city's largest-footfall Puja, claiming 1.5-2 lakh visitors; its five-day cultural festival is branded 'Sammad'. Won the Senco Sharod Samman 2018 for ambience and crowd management. Caution, a separate 'Sarathi Cultural Association' with a different Koramangala venue also exists - do not merge the two. Mangala Kalyana Mantapa, 80 ft Road near Forum Mall, KHB 7th Block, Koramangala Kolaj Socio-Cultural Trust, Koramangala 2010 Deliberately 'ghoroa' - homely and intimate rather than mega-scale. Strongly concept-driven idols, e.g. Durga as ascetic Brahmacharini rather than warrior. Free entry, no parking. No standalone website. Sri Krishna Temple, near Jyothi Nivas College, Koramangala, Bengaluru 560034 Whitefield Cultural Association (WCA) 2003 Runs the trademarked 'Whitefield Durga Puja'. Registered under the Government of Karnataka, with an explicit CSR arm in education, healthcare and environment. The family-oriented East Bengaluru Puja. Whitefield; 2025 venue Palm Meadows, near Mahaveer Tranquil SORRBA - Sarjapur Outer Ring Road Bengali Association 2008 (news-sourced, not primary) Formed by Bengali families living around the junction of Sarjapur Road and the Outer Ring Road. Heavy on Bengali theatre productions and Kolkata street-food stalls alongside the Puja. The 2008 date is from a 2015 Citykemp feature; SORRBA's own site does not state a year. Sarjapur Road; 2025 venue Samskruti Pavilion Convention Centre, Sulikunte BARSHA - Bengali Association for HSR and Sarjapur, Bangalore December 2014 Its own about page says 'We started our journey in December, 2014', corroborated by Karnataka society registration number JNR-S344-2014-15. Aggregators variously claim 2016 and 2019 - both appear wrong. Grew from 20 to 125 members; runs Rabindra-Nazrul Jayanti at The HSR Club; CSR work with Samarthanam Trust. BARSHA Durga Puja Ground, opposite TCIS School, HSR Extension / Haralur, off Sarjapur Road ECCA - Electronic City Cultural Association 2012 The IT-corridor Puja, run largely by tech-professional volunteers; a registered charitable organisation formed in 2012, with its first Sarvajanin Durgotsav the same year. Large award haul. No official website - a page at sumandeyashi.github.io is a personal build, not ECCA's site. White Feather Convention Centre, near NICE Toll Gate, Electronic City Sanskritik Bengali Association Bangalore c. 2013-2014 (approximate; site says 'Celebrating 11 Glorious Years' but gives no year) This is the real organisation behind what people call 'Sanskriti Bangalore' - no body of that exact name exists. A non-profit trust started by South Bangalore families; won Sharod Samman Best Theme Puja 2018 and Best Venue Branding 2018. Founding year approximate. Elite Banquet Hall, Puttenahalli Road, JP Nagar Phase 6, Bengaluru 560078 Anandadhara Bangalore Conflicting, founded 2011 (Citykemp 2015) or registered 2012 (other sources) Explicitly themed around rural Bengal rather than urban spectacle. Founded around 2011 and registered the following year, by the accounts available. JP Nagar, South Bengaluru R T Nagar Bengali Socio Cultural Trust (R T Nagar Sarbajanin Durga Puja Samiti) 2006 The Palace Grounds Puja. One of the few that runs Jagadhatri Puja as well as Saraswati, Durga, Kali and Lakshmi. Blood-donation camps, hosts around 50 NGO children, wheelchair access for seniors, and its own mobile app. 'R T Nagar Bengali Association' and the Samiti are the same body, not two organisations. Puja at Palace Grounds, Gate 9 (Princess Green), Bellary Road; registered at No. 17, 10th Cross, Manorayanapalya, Sultanpalya Main Road, R T Nagar PO, Bengaluru 560032 Oikotan Hebbal Cultural Society 2013 Runs all four Pujas - Durga, Kali, Lakshmi and Saraswati. Repeat winner of best-theme awards; named by Deccan Herald among 2025's notable pandals. The domain oikotan.in only redirects to Facebook, so the Facebook page is the real address. Hebbal, North Bengaluru Kaggadasapura Bengali Association (KBA) 15 August 2007 Claims 6,500+ members. Its Puja is branded 'Sharad Utsav'. Notable for us because its catchment, C V Raman Nagar, is named after the same physicist who founded RRI and directed IISc. V K Sports Convention Hall, Malleshpalya; serves Kaggadasapura and C V Raman Nagar Bengali in Bangalore (BinB) 2004 Started as an online Bengali community and is unusually broad, BinB Sports (badminton, table tennis, a football league, gully cricket), BinB JobMart, and Kannada Rajyotsava alongside the Bengali calendar. Deccan Herald covered its 15th Durgotsav, honouring Tagore. The 2004 date is on its membership page, not its homepage. Durgotsav at